{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And Moshe said, Thus says YHWH.</b> This prophecy was spoken to him while he stood before Pharaoh — for once he had gone out from before him, he never again saw his face." "<b>At midnight.</b> As the night was divided. <b>כחצת.</b> Like ״בַּעֲלוֹת״ (I Kings 18), ״בַּחֲרוֹת אַפָּם בָּנוּ״ (Psalms 124) — this is its plain sense for one who studies it on its face: חֲצוֹת is not a noun meaning 'half.' And our Sages interpreted it as כַּחֲצִי הַלַּיְלָה, 'about midnight,' and they said that Moshe said ״כַּחֲצוֹת״ — which implies near it, either before it or after it — and did not say ״בַּחֲצוֹת״ lest Pharaoh's astrologers err and say Moshe is a liar (Berakhot 4)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:51:28.742616521Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}